    "body": "claimed: main session (review fixes for PR #65) · 2026-11-07T10:23Z · branch issue/62-lathe-spindle-refusal · plan: independent review found two blocking holes - (1) the check runs only at generation; a work offset moved in Y afterwards leaves the op fresh and posts every diameter 2 mm small - re-check at post time with the live origin (and/or stamp the slot's origin); (2) the tolerance bounds axis drift over height but not lean x radius on faces (a 1 mm x R40 washer can post a 0.04 mm cone) - bound the full displacement over the part's extent. Plus: fit noise on non-uniform tessellation vs the 0.5 um tolerance, a Y-offset turning test, boundary tests, non-G54 slot test, wording.",
